  {
   "id": "wq9A3cCtKwAJ",
   "from": "Fong Chun Chan",
   "author": "61221ab1f726dce8",
   "date": "2016-05-17T15:48:25Z",
   "subject": "Re: Nvim-R: Syntax Highlighting Not Working in Rmarkdown Chunks",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I just installed neovim on mac using homebrew (<a href=\"https://github.com/neovim/homebrew-neovim/blob/master/README.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/neovim/homebrew-neovim/blob/master/README.md&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494115881000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0cT1-zW46u37r_h-BaUYiq\">https://github.com/neovim/homebrew-neovim/blob/master/README.md</a>)<br><br><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">brew install neovim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">neovim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">neovim</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>Did the minimalist vim setup you suggested and it works now! I think there is something up with the vim version that I can&#39;t explain...perhaps I will just finally make the switch over to neovim. I can&#39;t live without this plugin and the syntax highlighting :)</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "_VRLXWeyKwAJ",
   "from": "Jakson Alves de Aquino",
   "author": "b256a2742aacd200",
   "date": "2016-05-17T17:13:38Z",
   "subject": "Re: Nvim-R: Syntax Highlighting Not Working in Rmarkdown Chunks",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>You could copy your old vimrc to .config/nvim/init.vim because it may work without the need of any change. But, if there is any problem, you could slice your old vimrc in many pieces and add them one by one to your new .config/nvim/init.vim. After adding each piece, you should test if the syntax highlight of R Markdown is OK.</div><div><br></div><div>If any of your plugins use Python, you have to install Python support. See:</div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">h nvim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">python</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
